<title>UK: BAA says 1996 airport traffic up 5.5 pct.</title>
<headline>BAA says 1996 airport traffic up 5.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>British airports operator BAA Plc said traffic in calendar 1996 rose 5.5 percent compared with the previous year to 96.8 million passengers. The number of flights using BAA airports increased with total air movements up 5.4 percent at 966,700.</p>
<p>Cargo tonnage was up 5.0 percent to 1.46 million tonnes.  </p>
<p>In December, the company's seven UK airports handled a total of 7.1 million passengers, up 7.8 percent on the same month last year.</p>
<p>Passenger traffic at London Heathrow increased by 5.8 percent to 4.3 million passengers and by 11.3 percent to 1.6 million passengers at London Gatwick.</p>
<p>Passenger numbers were up 4.4 pct for the first nine months of BAA's financial year to March 31.</p>
